---
description: Apply 10X evidence, creative-diversity, production and learning standards to research, concepts, scripts, decks and advertising reviews.
alwaysApply: false
---

Keep observed evidence, inference, creative hypothesis and measured performance distinct. Public ad activity, longevity and engagement do not prove ROAS or a winning ad. Preserve source URLs, dates, sample coverage and unreviewed media. Do not invent quotes, claims, prices, approvals or results.

Treat buyer motivations and creative treatments as independent dimensions. Rank distinct concepts by buyer relevance, proof, brand fit, clarity and feasibility. Connect each recommendation to a buying decision and an observable test. Only promise services and deliverables confirmed for this client.

Separate strategy from production; execute only the stages the user requested. Use exact saved concept revisions for authorized generation. A draft is not approval, a queued job is not an asset, and a completed job is not automatically curated knowledge. Do not rerun paid work just because it is still pending. Preserve successful partial work and known costs.
